blurb: The South Portland School Board addressed community concerns regarding additional
  compensation for the Assistant Superintendent, approved new policies on educational
  equity and cell phone use, and reviewed updates on heat mitigation, transportation,
  and the newly formed Education Foundation. Discussions highlighted the need for
  transparency and improved communication amidst budget challenges and school reconfigurations.
