summary:
- topic: Assistant Superintendent Compensation
  text: The Board Chair provided a detailed justification for the $12,000 additional
    compensation to Assistant Superintendent Jo Prince, citing her extensive work
    on the budget, new labor contracts, HR functions, and elementary school reconfiguration
    during a tumultuous year. Funding was sourced from prorated new superintendent
    salary and business office savings.
- topic: Student Representative Introduction and School Updates
  text: New student representative Sarah Lupien introduced herself, highlighting her
    long history in the district and commitment to student perspective. She then provided
    a comprehensive report on end-of-year activities, celebrations, and athletic achievements
    across all South Portland schools.
- topic: Education Foundation Update
  text: Sarah Stickney presented an update on the newly incorporated Education Foundation,
    which aims to support the community school strategy. The foundation is building
    its board, developing fundraising plans, and will focus on academic achievement
    and belonging programs.
- topic: PBIS Awards at SPHS
  text: Sarah Glenn, SPHS Principal, detailed the first year of the Positive Behavior
    Interventions and Supports (PBIS) program, 'The Red Riot Way.' Quarterly assemblies
    recognized students for being responsible, engaged, safe, and respectful, with
    support from local businesses.
- topic: Heat Mitigation and Transportation Plans
  text: Mike Nalli, Director of Operations and Safety, outlined a heat mitigation
    plan including AC and fan deployment based on temperature thresholds. He also
    addressed track team and Brickhill bus overcrowding, detailing measures taken
    and future plans with a third-party consultant to optimize routes and capacity.
- topic: Public Comment on Board Decisions and Transparency
  text: Several community members and teachers expressed disappointment and concern
    regarding the Assistant Superintendent's compensation, citing a lack of transparency
    and perceived inconsistency with budget cuts and staff reductions. They also raised
    ongoing issues with busing and the need for better public notice of board meetings.
- topic: Policy Approvals
  text: The board unanimously approved the Agenda Policy (BEDB), the Educational Equity
    Policy, and the first reading of an amended Cell Phone Policy (JICI) which will
    prohibit cell phone use during the school day. Discussions emphasized the importance
    of community engagement in developing procedures for the cell phone policy.
