      safety risks than keeping them in a warm school, aligning with winter weather
      protocols.
  - seconds: 3170
    speaker: George Risch
    text: George Risch expressed appreciation for the plan and asked if such a plan
      existed before. Mike Nalli admitted previous plans were less formalized and
      that the district was caught off guard by early hot weather, leading to the
      current, more proactive approach with increased AC unit inventory.
